{"name":"Seafoam Whisper","hex":"#a1bdbf","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"seafoam","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A foam created by the agitation of seawater.","A light green-blue color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seafoam"},{"term":"whisper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of speaking in a quiet voice, especially without vibration of the vocal cords; the sound thus produced.","A rumor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To speak softly or under one's breath, so as to be heard only by one near at hand; to utter words without sonant breath; to talk without that vibration of the vocal cords which gives sonorous, or vocal, sound.","To say (something) softly or under one's breath, so as to be heard only by one near at hand; to utter (something) without sonant breath, without that vibration of the vocal cords which gives sonorous, or vocal, sound."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whisper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sea foam","blocks":[{"text":"Sea foam, ocean foam, beach foam, or spume is a type of foam created by the agitation of seawater, particularly when it contains higher concentrations of dissolved organic matter derived from sources such as the offshore breakdown of algal blooms. These compounds can act as surfactants or foaming agents. As the seawater is churned by breaking waves in the surf zone adjacent to the shore, the surfactants under these turbulent conditions trap air, forming persistent bubbles that stick to each other through surface tension."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Sea_foam_at_Ocean_Beach_in_San_Francisco_-1_on_3-25-11.jpg/330px-Sea_foam_at_Ocean_Beach_in_San_Francisco_-1_on_3-25-11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_foam"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Sea_foam_at_Ocean_Beach_in_San_Francisco_-1_on_3-25-11.jpg/500px-Sea_foam_at_Ocean_Beach_in_San_Francisco_-1_on_3-25-11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Sea_foam_at_Ocean_Beach_in_San_Francisco_-1_on_3-25-11.jpg/1280px-Sea_foam_at_Ocean_Beach_in_San_Francisco_-1_on_3-25-11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Sea_foam_at_Ocean_Beach_in_San_Francisco_-1_on_3-25-11.jpg/500px-Sea_foam_at_Ocean_Beach_in_San_Francisco_-1_on_3-25-11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sea foam washed up or blown onto a beach","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASea_foam_at_Ocean_Beach_in_San_Francisco_-1_on_3-25-11.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Sea_spray_sea_foam_connection.png/500px-Sea_spray_sea_foam_connection.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Sea_spray_sea_foam_connection.png/1280px-Sea_spray_sea_foam_connection.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Sea_spray_sea_foam_connection.png/500px-Sea_spray_sea_foam_connection.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Connection between sea foam and sea spray formation. The dark orange line indicates processes common to the formation of both sea spray and sea foam.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASea_spray_sea_foam_connection.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Brandung_%28MW_2015.02.27.%29.JPG/500px-Brandung_%28MW_2015.02.27.%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Brandung_%28MW_2015.02.27.%29.JPG/1280px-Brandung_%28MW_2015.02.27.%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Brandung_%28MW_2015.02.27.%29.JPG/500px-Brandung_%28MW_2015.02.27.%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sea foam usually contains a mixture of decomposed organic materials","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrandung_(MW_2015.02.27.).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Plankton_creates_sea_foam_2.jpg/500px-Plankton_creates_sea_foam_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Plankton_creates_sea_foam_2.jpg/1280px-Plankton_creates_sea_foam_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Plankton_creates_sea_foam_2.jpg/500px-Plankton_creates_sea_foam_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Bubbles of plankton-enriched foam left in a tide pool after high tide","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlankton_creates_sea_foam_2.jpg"}],"sounds":{"whisper":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9b/En-us-whisper.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9b/En-us-whisper.ogg/En-us-whisper.ogg.mp3"}]}}}